  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: Multi-profile RNA with scvi_n200 is the strongest setup (config_005: 0.650 acc, config_006: 0.653 acc), and aggregation choice (avgpool vs transformer) has negligible impact (~0.3% difference). Image-only models are very weak (~0.21-0.23 acc), raising the question of whether image adds any value when fused with the strong RNA signal. Question: Does adding the image modality (resnet50) to the best RNA multi-profile configuration (scvi_n200, avgpool) improve validation accuracy over the RNA-only baseline of ~0.650, or does it dilute the signal? This is the minimal multimodal extension of config_005—only adding image_encoder and fusion (concat, the simplest option)—so it cleanly isolates the contribution of the image modality. Why this is the best next experiment: Before investing budget in optimizing fusion type, image encoder, or aggregation within the multimodal space, we need to know whether image contributes at all. If config_030 matches or beats 0.650, we have a strong direction to exploit; if it underperforms, we save budget by ruling out the image modality and focusing on RNA-only refinements. Starting with the simpler resnet50 and concat fusion keeps the experiment interpretable."
}

